    "result_text": "The test passes. Let me verify the full-stack change is complete and consistent.\n\nThe change is implemented as a small, additive full-stack slice:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V12__tasks.sql`: a new `tasks` table (`id`, `project_id` FK \u2192 `projects`, `title`, `done` boolean defaulting to open), following the same identity-by-default convention as `projects` so the test seed can supply explicit fixture ids.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor)** \u2014 two new endpoints, each a new YAML + logic class, both under `/api/`:\n- `GET /api/tasks?projectId=<id>` (`ListTasks`) \u2014 lists a project's tasks oldest-first.\n- `POST /api/tasks/{id}/toggle` (`ToggleTask`) \u2014 flips the `done` flag and records the side-effect through the `Audit` service (`TASK_DONE`/`TASK_REOPENED id=<n>`), matching the invoice pay/send precedent.\n- New `Task` entity, `TaskRepository`, `TaskView`.\n- `TestSupportController` extended to seed `tasks` (via `JdbcTemplate` with explicit fixture ids) and to `TRUNCATE tasks RESTART IDENTITY` on reset.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 the projects feature's `ProjectDetail` now loads and renders a `project-tasks-table` with `task-row-<id>` rows (`task-title`, `task-status` showing `OPEN`/`DONE`) and a `task-toggle-<id>` button that ticks a task off and reloads. It composes into the existing feature file \u2014 no edits to the router or other features.\n\nAll `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly, and `bin/e2e` passes.",
